    "Complete continuous occupied two-storey left/right wings with both third-floor roof terraces. Only central rooms/stair and finite right side room are third-storey solid; no full-width third storey, no invented roof tower or basement.",
    "671 opposite upper-side projecting foyer remains one storey and separate from photographed668 lower-side main entrance. Shared stair/column translations671(-21,-12),672master,673(-16,-1) preserve similar column pitch instead of rescaling whole pages.",
    "First-review correction is complete: raw671 double-door line y279 maps to master267, not corridor north line247. Corrected finite entrance recess and floor-reaching vertically divided door proxy with upper transom replace an ordinary low-transom window. Entry glass and forward mullion first-hit rays independently distinguish267.6 and268.4 exterior surfaces.",
    "668 continuous pale vertical fins, opaque muted-red spandrels, tall upper/lower glazing bands, broad grounded stair and canopy are recognizable. Rounded original canopy fascia is explicitly simplified as a thick rectangular edge. No lettering, air-conditioning or fine hardware reconstruction claimed.",
    "669 is tree-obscured local white-wall/window/turquoise-canopy evidence. The same-mesh view is a bounded local central-side candidate, not proof of the unique end, full opposite facade, unseen upper bay count or camera recovery.",
    "Unknown rear windows remain neutral; absolute dimensions/heights, window spacing, colors and limited grade are approximate. Occupied rooms are solid exterior proxies, not surveyed interior circulation. No whole garden, trees, neighboring building or campus terrain added.",
    "Seven per-face opaque material groups and canonical STL/3MF/native mesh agree exactly in original coordinates/order/winding/material assignments. No photographs, source-plan/PDF/overlay pixels or textures embedded."
